}
System.out.println(list);
```', '{"A":"[4, 2]","B":"[4, 7, 2, 9]","C":"[]","D":"[7, 9]"}', 'D', NULL, 'Backward delete-by-condition removes elements < 5 (the 2 and the 4), leaving `[7, 9]` in order. Backward traversal avoids skips.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-u4-q17', 'ap_csa', '4.10', '4', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
